  "text": "I'll read the brief and the guidance index first, then only the skills that review actually needs.The brief is a read-only design consensus. I'll load the design method, the React Bits Pro catalog, and the pages he named.The auth catalog file is not there, so I will judge login from the skill and the pages he named. Next I will look at those renders and the One and Deck code.RESULT: FINDINGS\n\nGrok. Pass 10 stays the base. `feed-open.png` is the story grid he called better, and beside `deck-feed.png` it is blank: no source list, no free-week meter, no this-week line, no Agent card, and a DM strip where a header should gather the page. `onboarding-step-1.png` repeats the left steps in the center and keeps the posts off the profile. `login.png` is Deck's form and Deck's stack with a gap between them. `sources.png` is four cards with counts, and a reason only where the fixture has focus text. One pass, Deck's pieces under the One, same theme.\n\n1. Feed chrome\nThe source list is its own button, first, at the bottom left. The page bubble stays beside it for Feed, Sources, Notifications, the account, and Sign out. He said the sidebar \"should be a button by itself, first thing,\" and that it \"can float atop the page.\" The panel floats over the stories and does not push them. Closed, it is gone: \"When it's closed, it's closed.\" Inside, Deck's groups, three rows, then Show more. Logo, company name, count, numbers in one column, group total included. \"The name/handle switch can be removed.\" The header is one bar: Feed, Clustered/Direct, the free-week meter (days left and the watched-post bar), Get alerts on X, and @farzanmrz. This week is one line under that bar, the story count and the day marks. One Agent card leads the stories: Live, the newest time, and the failed line. The amber checking bar shows only while a check is running. The three tiles stay off the top (\"Get rid of the three cards up top\"). No kind pills (\"I don't know\"). Story stacks stay the pass 10 grid. Astra may drop the names and leave logo plus count. Kimi may put Free week, Agent, and This week back in one row, and add the pills.\n\n2. Onboarding\nThe left column is the eight steps in `site/next/building/steps.ts`: Find your X profile, Read your newest posts, Gather candidates, Jev checks relevance, Choose sources, Search X for more accounts, Write your brief, Save your agent. \"The left side is for my timeline.\" One heading for the page: \"Choosing sources\" until that step finishes, then \"Saving your agent,\" then \"Your agent is ready.\" Top right the whole time: the X account chip for the typed handle, and Build my agent. After save, that button is Open your feed. The right column is \"the user's own stuff.\" Profile at the top. The pinned post stays off (\"You don't need to show the pinned post\"). Posts stream under \"Reading your newest posts,\" one after another, while that step runs. From Choose sources on, the brief is the first thing on the right. Center, Gather: the count climbs and the quoted-account chips arrive. Center, Check relevance: the checked bar fills, then chips settle into Strong match, Possible match, and Set aside, as on `deck-building.png`. From Choose sources on, the center is only the sources, grouped as accounts, sites, feeds, and GitHub. Setup keeps the handle and the sentence, then opens this page. Without a handle it waits. Connecting X is not required. The sample source list and sample stories leave setup. Astra may keep the pinned post. Kimi may retitle the page on every step.\n\n3. Login\nUse Deck's login as it stands in `deck-login.png`. He likes that one more, and \"separating the login from the cards is not nice.\" The form and the story stack share one stage, the stack against the form. `auth-1` through `auth-6` and `authentication-1` through `authentication-14` are full sign-in screens. No layout file was there, so no slug is named. A block would bring its own colors, and the skin stays DESIGN.md. The story cards stay Deck's stack, in that same stage. Astra may still drop `authentication-1` in and park the cards in its spare half.\n\n4. Sources page\nOne list. Group labels for X accounts, RSS feeds, Websites, and GitHub. An account row is logo, name, and @handle on one line, then Remove. A site, feed, or repo row is logo, name, and address on one line, then Remove. Add sits on the group label. No numbers on rows or groups: \"There should be no numbers next to the sources because this is the sources page.\" A click shows the reason under that row for every source. The Vercel-only line is the fixture. `sources.tsx` prints `focus` only when the sample has it, and the product has a reason for each chosen source. The only number on the page is the free-week pool, 300 watched X posts, once in the header. Sites and feeds are unlimited, so Add does not hit a source cap. \"At most ten websites and feeds\" is what onboarding recommends. No Settings page this pass. He is guessing. Subscription stays the free-week meter until the week ends and the plans show. Kimi may add Settings now, and an \"n of 10\" cap.\n\n5. Notifications\nThe same header as the other pages. The X DM row becomes one button, Message @oparax_ai. It opens X so he can DM the bot from his own account. There is no toggle: \"there won't be a toggle. There'll be a button.\" The line says alerts start when that account sends Start alerts. No made-up DM history under it. Astra may keep a switch beside the button.\n\n6. Live feed\nThis week, the product app on another port, with a real build for farzanmrz and one for Reshad. The lab replay is the script in `steps.ts`, 4.6 seconds of the same six stories. A longer replay is still those stories, and that is what is bugging him. oparax.ai waits until he has walked this pass. His time is one sitting: two handles, two sentences, both builds, then each feed. Astra may lengthen the lab replay so the walk needs no second app.\n\n7. Order\nOne Opus builder. Feed, then Onboarding, then Login, then Sources, then Notifications, then Setup. He walks localhost in product order: Login, Setup, Onboarding, Feed, Sources, Notifications. Ask him two things. Does the sidebar row keep the company name beside the logo, or logo and count only? Do the kind pills stay off?",
